i":44.4,"_gate_spread":0.042881474861117236,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":21.4,"_gate_roic_consistency":2.851007450993493,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.03930628839540592,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":20.2,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":0.13275048403633583,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":91.4,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0.07061130134263197,"_gp_fund_growth":true,"_score_fund_growth":70.6,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0005763707112606865,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.8,"_gate_share_shrink":0.015481263692813885,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":30.6,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.006159140486050659,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":89.7,"_gate_insider_own":0.32415,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Live Nation Entertainment, Inc. operates as a live entertainment company worldwide. The company operates through Concerts, Ticketing, and Sponsorship & Advertising segments. Its Concerts segment promotes live music events in its owned or operated venues, and in rented third-party venues. This segment operates and manages music venues; produces music festivals; creates associated content; and offers management and other services to artists. The Ticketing segment manages the ticketing operations, including the provision of ticketing software and services to consumers with marketplace for tickets and event information through mobile apps, other websites, and retail outlets, as well as its websites, such as livenation.com and ticketmaster.com; and provides ticket resale services. This segment offers ticketing services for arenas, stadiums, amphitheaters, music clubs, concert promoters, professional sports franchises and leagues, college sports teams, performing arts venues, museums, and theaters. Its Sponsorship & Advertising segment sells international, national, and local sponsorships and placement of advertising, including signage, online advertising, and promotional programs; rich media offering, including advertising related with live streaming and music-related content; and ads through distribution network of venues, events, and websites. This segment also manages the development of strategic sponsorship programs, as well as develops, books, and produces custom events or programs for specific brands. It owns, operates, or leases entertainment venues. The company was formerly known as Live Nation, Inc. and changed its name to Live Nation Entertainment, Inc. in January 2010. Live Nation Entertainment, Inc. was incorporated in 2005 and is headquartered in Beverly Hills, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Michael  Rapino | President, CEO & Director | Age 59 | Compensation: $22.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 17K people. Revenue per employee of $1.4M ranks in the top quartile among Communication Services peers, improving at 12%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $19K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $9K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 16\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Live Nation Entertainment, Inc. is a large-cap communication services business with a $40.8B market cap on $25.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +15% over the past three years and +13% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 14% against a 9% cost of capital, a 4-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $334M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 1 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.81\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 4.0\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 0.1%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 32% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.2\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 183% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.8330054730018321},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (15.4% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Communication Services ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"AI-generated content commoditisation \u2014 as creation costs collapse toward zero, content libraries lose pricing power and differentiation narrows.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Growing faster than most Communication Services peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"What Does Live Nation Entertainment (LYV) Record Q3 Mean For Its Global Growth?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/media/nyse-lyv/live-nation-entertainment/news/what-does-live-nation-entertainment-lyv-record-q3-mean-for-i","date":"2026-11-07","timestamp":1794011600.713,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.92,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Live Nation Entertainment Inc (LYV) (Q3 2026) Earnings Call Highlights: Record Attendance and ...","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/live-nation-entertainment-inc-lyv-091700546.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793956620.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.802,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Live Nation (LYV) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/live-nation-lyv-q3-2026-074900000.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793951855.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.382,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Live Nation outlines close to 180M concert fans in 2026 as Ticketmaster targets high single-digit AOI growth (NYSE:LYV)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4667609-live-nation-outlines-close-to-180m-concert-fans-in-2026-as-ticketmaster-targets-high-single","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793922421.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.214,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Live Nation (NYSE:LYV) beats expectations in strong Q3 2026","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/live-nation-nyse-lyv-beats-230654791.html","dat